---
import HomeLayout from "../layouts/HomeLayout.astro";
import ButtonDemo from "../components/ButtonDemo.astro";
import LinkButton from "../components/LinkButton.astro";
---

<HomeLayout
  title="Kimak"
  description="Headless UI primitives. React-first. Framework-agnostic kernel."
>
  <p class="eyebrow">Headless UI</p>
  <div class="hero">
    <h1>Behavior in the kernel. Look in your CSS.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Kimak owns keyboard, focus, and ARIA. Spec is the contract. React is the first adapter. Vue
      and Svelte ship Button in lockstep. Style with anatomy selectors — or opt into the Tailwind
      plugin.
    </p>
    <div class="hero-actions">
      <LinkButton href="/docs/getting-started">Get started</LinkButton>
      <LinkButton href="/docs/components/button" variant="outline">View Button</LinkButton>
    </div>
  </div>

  <ButtonDemo />

  <h2>Package graph</h2>
  <div class="package-graph">
    <div>@kimak/spec → @kimak/core → adapters → @kimak/ui-*</div>
    <div>@kimak/spec → @kimak/tailwind</div>
    <div>@kimak/spec → @kimak/motion-gsap</div>
  </div>
  <p class="muted">
    The portable surface is <code>connect()</code>, not JSX. Product sugar lives in
    <code>@kimak/ui-*</code>. Look never enters the machine.
  </p>
</HomeLayout>
